.TH FREAD 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fread \- read items from a Crunch file stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t fread(void* " buffer ", size_t " size ", size_t " count ", struct FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads up to
.I count
items of
.I size
bytes into the buffer. A partial final item may modify the buffer but does not
count as a complete item. A zero size or count returns zero without I/O.
.PP
End-of-file and errors are recorded in the stream. End-of-file remains set
until a successful
.BR fseek (3crunch)
or
.BR clearerr (3crunch).
Use
.BR feof (3crunch)
and
.BR ferror (3crunch)
to distinguish end-of-file from an error.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of complete items read. A short count can mean end-of-file
or an error. On error
.B errno
is set; a null nonempty buffer or stream sets
.BR EINVAL .
A size/count product exceeding the supported signed 64-bit byte range sets
.BR EOVERFLOW .
.SH NOTES
I/O is unbuffered; interrupted reads report an error.
Crunch streams are not C library
.B FILE
objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fopen (3crunch),
.BR clearerr (3crunch),
.BR feof (3crunch),
.BR ferror (3crunch),
.BR fseek (3crunch),
.BR fwrite (3crunch),
.BR read (3crunch)
